            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cut this recipe in half down to 16 servings. Instead of using 1 1/2 eggs, I used two full eggs. I did have to add a little more oil than what was asked for because using half wheat flour made it drier than I think it would have been had I used all AP flour. I made this into muffins instead of one big loaf. I did not get 16 muffins, I got eleven and they were on the smaller side. Before baking, I sprinkled each muffin mound with a little cinnamon sugar. Very nice, basic zucchini bread recipe. It reminds me a lot of the one my Mom made when I was a child."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I scaled the recipe in half and baked in two USA Pan mini loaf pans (6x3-1/2 inches) for 43 minutes. Followed the recipe to the letter and wouldn’t change a thing. However, I did sprinkle a little cinnamon sugar on the top before baking. They baked up beautifully, the bread was very moist and tender with just enough sweetness to be satisfying. This is good zucchini bread.",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-31T12:38:56.044Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
